      "value": "@{5d458c2bce0d0218577b8c24|full_name}: Actually, I just realized why this is happening before I even saved your picture. The image gets sent through the cropper during the upload process, even if you don't touch any of the controls. Once you move onto the next stage of the uploading process, the cropper will duplicate the image, applying the needed transformations, which in this case is none, but is likely resulting in a much higher-sized image buffer being sent to the API.\nI'll create a bug ticket for this internally, but as a workaround for the moment, you should be able to downsize your image a bit below 4k to get through the issue.\nThanks for the help in finding a super weird edge case!",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
